WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:04.819
Let's get into audience questions for the
week, our first host.

00:00:04.819 --> 00:00:09.940
Trump set of questions in the Joe Biden era.

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:14.950
There's something in the air that's just seeming
a little different, but let's get right into

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:15.950
it.

00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:20.200
And a lot of these questions really go to
sort of seeking to understand where we are

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:21.430
as a country right now.

00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:23.890
And I think that these all tie together very
well.

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:24.940
The first one is David.

00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:31.960
Now, with Trump in the rear view, how did
Trump change the country and how did he not?

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:36.079
And I think this is really the perfect question
to start to understand what happened.

00:00:36.079 --> 00:00:46.270
Donald Trump did not, as as near as I can
tell, create racists or racism, create xenophobes

00:00:46.270 --> 00:00:51.170
who want to stop immigration from so-called
asshole countries.

00:00:51.170 --> 00:00:57.100
What he did was he coalesced these groups
of people and he made them more comfortable

00:00:57.100 --> 00:00:59.039
being public about it.

00:00:59.039 --> 00:01:04.699
The things that used to be whispered behind
closed doors by people who had some sense

00:01:04.699 --> 00:01:08.729
that while this is what I believe, I recognize
I'll probably be looked down upon in most

00:01:08.729 --> 00:01:10.960
circles if I say it out loud.

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:15.690
They were welcomed into saying these things
out loud.

00:01:15.690 --> 00:01:19.510
But it's important to understand that that
is a change.

00:01:19.510 --> 00:01:25.609
Not not creating racism may be an area where
there was not a change under Trump, but the

00:01:25.609 --> 00:01:29.659
racism being more open is a change under Donald
Trump.

00:01:29.659 --> 00:01:35.680
And along those lines, the changes we really
saw under Trump include, of course, degrading

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:42.090
the public discourse, degrading what counts
as acceptable political debate, and what counts

00:01:42.090 --> 00:01:48.719
as acceptable in a political campaign in terms
of particular types of insults, not only about

00:01:48.719 --> 00:01:56.249
your political opponents, but, you know, ridiculing
disabilities, ridiculing deceased members

00:01:56.249 --> 00:01:57.310
of the military.

00:01:57.310 --> 00:02:01.689
There was nothing beyond the pale.

00:02:01.689 --> 00:02:08.280
It was beyond the pale that there was nothing
that Trump saw as off the table.

00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:14.350
I think better said in terms of what and how
you can criticize others and the change Trump

00:02:14.350 --> 00:02:15.350
made.

00:02:15.350 --> 00:02:16.520
And we'll see if it gets changed again.

00:02:16.520 --> 00:02:19.420
But it could be an irreversible change.

00:02:19.420 --> 00:02:24.170
Trump removed whatever was left of the idea
of American exceptionalism.

00:02:24.170 --> 00:02:30.750
We really sucked during the last four years
in ways that many Americans wrongly but many

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:35.430
Americans previously thought would only happen
in other countries or only happened in other

00:02:35.430 --> 00:02:36.430
countries.

00:02:36.430 --> 00:02:41.160
And it turns out that what we learned is that
the United States is just like any other place,

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:46.370
really terrible, corrupt people can get into
power, that corruption and weaponization can

00:02:46.370 --> 00:02:49.820
get into law enforcement, it can get into
the military.

00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:52.280
It can get into all aspects of government.

00:02:52.280 --> 00:02:53.570
It can interfere with science.

00:02:53.570 --> 00:02:58.910
It can infect even, you know, NASA and all
of these other things.

00:02:58.910 --> 00:03:00.210
And that is a change.

00:03:00.210 --> 00:03:09.660
Now, the things that didn't change during
Trump's presidency are also cause for concern.

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:10.970
What do I mean by that?

00:03:10.970 --> 00:03:16.600
Well, how did Trump get to be the Republican
nominee and ultimately become president?

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:24.430
The structure of anti intellectual ism and
reactionary politics, not based, in fact,

00:03:24.430 --> 00:03:27.200
are partially what got Donald Trump into power.

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:30.400
That hasn't changed is in fact, I would argue
it's worse than ever.

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:34.720
And it's been particularly weaponized by the
explosion of right wing extreme media like

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:39.480
Newsmax and on and Funen stuff and others.

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:43.070
The Electoral College got Trump into power.

00:03:43.070 --> 00:03:44.640
That hasn't changed.

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:47.770
So another Trump could come into power again.

00:03:47.770 --> 00:03:52.920
I think if there is, what is the most important
message that could be taken away from the

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:53.920
Trump presidency?

00:03:53.920 --> 00:04:00.291
Because there are many checks and balances
aren't nearly as robust as we thought they

00:04:00.291 --> 00:04:01.291
were.

00:04:01.291 --> 00:04:06.340
When you have a madman in the White House
and know we have all these different takeaways.

00:04:06.340 --> 00:04:12.650
The most important takeaway now that we're
looking forward must be nothing has changed

00:04:12.650 --> 00:04:15.340
about what got Trump into power in the first
place.

00:04:15.340 --> 00:04:21.180
If anything, it's worse, as we saw by 75 million
people voting for Trump in November.

00:04:21.180 --> 00:04:25.200
And just as easily as Trump got in, I would
argue it is even easier for another Trump

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:26.870
to get into power.

00:04:26.870 --> 00:04:28.520
That's the top takeaway.

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:35.220
So, yes, fixed gerrymandering, get rid of
the Electoral College, find a way to democratize

00:04:35.220 --> 00:04:39.910
the Senate, which is so anti-democratic, you've
got to deal with campaign finance, put dealing

00:04:39.910 --> 00:04:45.030
with climate into the law rather than leaving
it to the whims of political administrations.

00:04:45.030 --> 00:04:47.950
There's such a long list of things that have
to be done.

00:04:47.950 --> 00:04:55.320
But if we don't recognize that until we actually
deal with the culture that got Trump into

00:04:55.320 --> 00:05:00.620
a position where he could win the Republican
primary and eventually to the presidency,

00:05:00.620 --> 00:05:01.620
it could happen again.

00:05:01.620 --> 00:05:03.040
And that's very, very scary.

